This sample shows how to call GetGetsAsync and parse the result.

Uri endpoint = new Uri("<https://my-service.azure.com>");
CollaborationClient client = new CollaborationClient(endpoint);

Response response = await client.GetGetsAsync(null, null);

JsonElement result = JsonDocument.Parse(response.ContentStream).RootElement;
Console.WriteLine(result[0].ToString());

This sample shows how to call GetGetsAsync with all parameters and parse the result.

Uri endpoint = new Uri("<https://my-service.azure.com>");
CollaborationClient client = new CollaborationClient(endpoint);

Response response = await client.GetGetsAsync(true, null);

JsonElement result = JsonDocument.Parse(response.ContentStream).RootElement;
Console.WriteLine(result[0].GetProperty("collaborationId").ToString());
Console.WriteLine(result[0].GetProperty("collaborationName").ToString());
Console.WriteLine(result[0].GetProperty("userStatus").ToString());

